68 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186507968 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "44b72334-231e-5d57-bdc0-d2fb9585f9c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186507793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186507731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508030 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f962e375-138e-5ba3-a11f-61cf507ac9c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186507968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74956" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508060 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508060 #edb/ref 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "462f5046-e4ee-5f94-8bfd-00082400022c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508060 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1}=\\frac{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}-1)(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}\\frac{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (0,0)}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}+1) & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+1}+1 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1}+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508069 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508069 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129401" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508069 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508069 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine ${lim}_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508069 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6b2bedc8-52f9-5d40-afcd-8617235afd0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508069 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & =\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{1-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nLet's attempt to evaluate the limit approaching $(1,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Taking $x\\to (1,0)$ along the path $y=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,0)\\,\\,\\,y=0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Taking $x\\to (1,0)$ along the path $x=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,0)\\,\\,\\,x=1}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}1 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (1,0)}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-1}=\\text{DNE}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508124 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186508140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508124 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3074aaf8-a64d-58be-886f-5f8b626d0bc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508124 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186508060 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508125 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186508167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508125 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "33d52943-cf7c-5ddf-bb1f-113936cfa6d5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508125 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186265716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508127 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186508124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508127 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3c399357-4d7f-55ba-a5f1-d7571818aae3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508127 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186344994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508140 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186508125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508140 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b2bc548-78f2-5e4e-b985-befdf65ed49c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508140 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508167 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ee66d94f-00d8-5e5e-84ff-35a7175f7dff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508167 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186508069 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
